## 4de7c8083804

**A4DE-1 — Reproduced generator-contract defect: advertised helpful controls are inert and unknown controls are accepted.** Against generator SHA-256 `63a7ccb108e0dcc6f514653e36842cd728504171802dc5df39af5bca11e9f639`, the source-bound probe used seed `20261020`, sample index `4`. Each paired call below returned the same 9×10 grid with marker cells `[(6,2,6),(6,3,5),(7,3,7)]` and the same grid hash:

- `palette_kind="warm"` versus `palette_kind="cool"`;
- helpful `texture="warm"` versus helpful `texture="cool"`;
- `anchor_corner=False` versus `anchor_corner=True`;
- `asymmetry_force=False` versus `asymmetry_force=True`;
- baseline versus an undeclared `misspelled_axis="accepted"` override.

As a control, `grid_h=7, grid_w=7` produced a 7×7 instance, so the probe can observe a genuinely consumed axis. The generated grids pass `self_check`; this is an override/dataset-diversity defect, not a claimed wrong Racket label. Exact inputs, full grids, hashes, self-check results, declared axes, and replay command are in `checks/audit/4de7c8083804/override_and_validator_probe.json`.

The isolated audit lint also fails on the same source because `RULE_HASH` is missing and warns that `position_bias` is not probed and `n_distinct_colors=3` is a singleton. See `checks/audit/4de7c8083804-lint/checks/4de7c8083804_audit_lint.log`. The optional audit task-test stage reports no task-local or selected frozen tests; see `checks/audit/4de7c8083804-task-tests.console.log`.

**Impact.** Callers can believe they are producing palette, anchoring, or asymmetry diversity while receiving byte-identical examples, and typoed controls silently succeed. Suggested repair: route every exact axis through typed `GenCtx` draws or remove/mark it diagnostic; reject unknown overrides; pin the verified canonical `RULE_HASH`; add focused override tests. Audited source was not edited.
